'''Star Seer''' is the [[Tho'ra Clan]]'s real-time astrology visualizer and sensor-fusion HUD. It overlays minute-by-minute astrological events on a wearer's field of view, fused with local magnetometric, electrostatic, barometric, and other environmental sensor data, and personalized to the wearer's [[natal chart]].

Star Seer is one of the three pillars of the [[Tho'ra Clan|Clan's]] operational software stack, alongside [[StarCom]] (cyber / command) and [[NavCom]] (navigation / tactical). It typically runs on a [[HelmKit]]-mounted display module.

== Function ==

Star Seer computes and displays:
* Continuous astrological angle calculations to sub-arc-second resolution.
* Personal natal-chart extrapolation onto the present moment (transits, progressions, returns).
* Timestream visualization: forward-projected event likelihood as a probability volume.
* Local sensor fusion: magnetometer, electrostatic field, barometer, accelerometer, GPS, ambient EM.
* Event prediction in a ''localized and personalized'' frame — not generic transit advisories.

== Use Cases ==

* '''Off-grid combat HUD''' — special-forces-grade tactical aid for navigating without electronic detection. The astrology and local-field-fusion provides predictive utility independent of GPS / radio.
* '''[[Resonant Pipeline|Resonant contact timing]]''' — picking the astrologically-supported window for an approach.
* '''Self-navigation''' — Tho'ra operators reading their own moment-to-moment best action.
* '''[[Resonant Finder]] feedback''' — Star Seer ground-truth telemetry feeds back into the central Finder model.

