== Versions and Variants ==

* '''Mk0''' — ''Phone Astrology HUD''. Existing astrology apps + custom overlay decals on cosplay helmets. Hand-held only.
* '''Mk1''' — ''HelmKit-mounted prototype''. Single-eye micro-OLED display, [[SynastryEngine]] back-end, basic sensor fusion (magnetometer + barometer). Bench-validated.
* '''Mk2''' — ''Field-trial unit''. Binocular AR display, full sensor pack, on-board GPU for local inference, hardened against EMI. Deployed to senior Tho'ra operators only.
* '''Mk3''' — ''Production HUD''. Ruggedized, [[Earth Alliance]] auxiliary-issued, integrated with [[NavCom]] for tactical overlay sharing.

== Interfaces ==

* '''Mount''': [[HelmKit]] standard rail / optical bay.
* '''Compute''': on-helm SoC (Mk1–Mk2); on-helm + cloud (Mk3, via [[Earth Intelligence Network]]).
* '''Data sources''': [[SynastryEngine]], on-board sensors, [[Resonant Finder]] downlink, [[Space Weather]] feeds.
* '''Display''': transparent OLED / waveguide optics; subtle, non-intrusive HUD.

== Sensor Fusion Detail ==

Local readings the HUD fuses with astrological state:
* '''Magnetometer''' — 3-axis, micro-Tesla resolution. Detects nearby magnetic anomalies, ferrous structures, and (at the high end) geomagnetic perturbation correlated with [[Space Weather]] events.
* '''Electrostatic''' — measures local atmospheric potential gradient. Correlates with [[Atmospheric Electricity]] and approaching storm cells.
* '''Barometric''' — absolute and rate-of-change pressure.
* '''IMU''' — accelerometer + gyro for head-tracking and dead-reckoning.
* '''Ambient EM''' — broadband RF environment scan.
* '''Ambient light + color temp''' — for HUD brightness adaptation and circadian feedback.

